# Agent Management Portal — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Build a Vellum.ai-style agent management portal at `/agent` that can be deployed as a standalone Vercel project. The portal integrates with the existing Flue runtime, supports MCP configs, skill management, Discord + Resend channels, Daytona/Vercel sandboxes, schedules, and observability.

---

## Architecture

### Route Structure (Standalone `/agent` project)

```
agent/
├── app/
│   ├── layout.tsx                    # Root layout with sidebar nav
│   ├── page.tsx                      # Dashboard / overview
│   ├── globals.css                   # Shared styles (import from main)
│   ├── agents/
│   │   ├── page.tsx                  # Agent list
│   │   ├── [id]/
│   │   │   ├── page.tsx              # Agent detail + chat
│   │   │   ├── config/page.tsx       # Agent configuration
│   │   │   └── runs/page.tsx         # Agent run history
│   │   └── new/page.tsx              # Create agent
│   ├── workflows/
│   │   ├── page.tsx                  # Workflow list
│   │   ├── [id]/page.tsx             # Workflow detail + runs
│   │   └── new/page.tsx              # Create workflow
│   ├── skills/
│   │   ├── page.tsx                  # Skill registry
│   │   └── [id]/page.tsx             # Skill detail
│   ├── mcp/
│   │   └── page.tsx                  # MCP server configuration
│   ├── channels/
│   │   └── page.tsx                  # Discord + Resend channels
│   ├── sandboxes/
│   │   └── page.tsx                  # Daytona + Vercel sandbox management
│   ├── schedules/
│   │   ├── page.tsx                  # Schedule list
│   │   └── [id]/page.tsx             # Schedule detail
│   ├── observability/
│   │   ├── page.tsx                  # Observability dashboard
│   │   └── runs/[id]/page.tsx        # Individual run trace
│   └── settings/
│       ├── page.tsx                  # General settings
│       └── security/page.tsx         # FIDO2/WebAuthn enrollment
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                           # Shared UI components (shadcn)
│   ├── sidebar-nav.tsx               # Main navigation sidebar
│   ├── agent-card.tsx                # Agent preview card
│   ├── agent-chat.tsx                # Interactive agent chat panel
│   ├── workflow-card.tsx             # Workflow preview card
│   ├── skill-card.tsx                # Skill preview card
│   ├── mcp-config-form.tsx           # MCP server config form
│   ├── channel-status.tsx            # Channel connection status
│   ├── sandbox-terminal.tsx          # Sandbox terminal emulator
│   ├── schedule-timeline.tsx         # Schedule timeline view
│   ├── observability-chart.tsx       # Metrics visualization
│   ├── run-trace.tsx                 # Run execution trace
│   └── webauthn-enroll.tsx           # FIDO2 enrollment component
├── lib/
│   ├── api.ts                        # Flue SDK client wrapper
│   ├── auth.ts                       # WebAuthn + session auth
│   └── types.ts                      # Shared TypeScript types
├── next.config.mjs
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
├── tailwind.config.ts
└── vercel.json                       # Standalone Vercel config
```

### Key Design Decisions

1. **Standalone deployment**: The `agent/` directory is a complete Next.js app that can be deployed to Vercel independently. It shares the same Flue API backend at `www.beaglabs.com/api/flue/`.

2. **Neobrutalist design**: Inherits the existing design system (black borders, orange accent, shadow utilities) from the main site.

3. **Flue SDK client**: Uses `@flue/sdk` to communicate with the Flue runtime API for agent management, workflow invocation, and run inspection.

4. **WebAuthn authentication**: Implements FIDO2/WebAuthn for zero-trust identity verification as the primary auth method, with better-auth session fallback.

---

## Implementation Phases

### Phase 1: Project Scaffolding + Core Layout
- Create `agent/` as a standalone Next.js 16 app
- Set up shared design tokens (globals.css, tailwind)
- Build sidebar navigation with all sections
- Create root layout with auth provider

### Phase 2: Agent Management
- Agent list page with cards showing status, model, last active
- Agent detail page with interactive chat (POST to `/api/flue/agents/:name/:id`)
- Agent configuration page (model, instructions, tools, skills)
- Agent creation flow with form wizard

### Phase 3: Workflow Management
- Workflow list with run status indicators
- Workflow detail with run history table
- Workflow invocation form (manual trigger)
- Run detail page with event timeline

### Phase 4: Skill Registry
- Skill list showing installed skills from `.agents/skills/`
- Skill detail with SKILL.md preview
- Enable/disable toggle per agent
- Install new skill (from npm package or GitHub)

### Phase 5: MCP Configuration
- MCP server connection form (name, URL, headers)
- Connected server list with health status
- Tool discovery preview from connected servers
- Per-agent MCP server assignment

### Phase 6: Channel Management
- Discord channel status + configuration
- Resend email channel status + configuration
- Channel health monitoring
- Message/activity feed from channels

### Phase 7: Sandbox Management
- Daytona sandbox list with status (running/stopped/error)
- Vercel Sandbox fallback configuration
- Sandbox creation/termination controls
- File browser + terminal emulator per sandbox

### Phase 8: Schedules
- Schedule list with cron expressions and next-run times
- Create/edit schedule form (workflow or agent dispatch)
- Schedule run history
- Enable/disable individual schedules

### Phase 9: Observability Dashboard
- Overview metrics (total runs, success rate, avg latency, cost)
- Run timeline chart (runs over time)
- Model usage breakdown (tokens, cost per model)
- Individual run trace viewer (events, tool calls, model turns)
- Error log aggregation

### Phase 10: Security (WebAuthn)
- FIDO2/WebAuthn enrollment flow
- Passkey management (list, add, remove)
- Session management
- Zero-trust identity verification integration

